Notebook[{
Cell["ChiEFT: build the UFO from ChiEFT.fr", "Title"],
Cell["This notebook reproduces the ChiEFT_UFO directory and param_card.dat from the FeynRules model file ChiEFT.fr. Keep it in the same folder as ChiEFT.fr and evaluate the cells from top to bottom.", "Text"],
Cell["Requirements: Mathematica and FeynRules 2.3.49 with feynrules/feynrules-2.3.49-chieft.patch applied (see README.md; stock FeynRules writes an unusable UFO). Tested with Mathematica 14.3. Python 3 is used in the last step to write the param card.", "Text"],
Cell["1. Load FeynRules", "Section"],
Cell["Edit the path below to point at your patched FeynRules installation.", "Text"],
Cell["$FeynRulesPath = SetDirectory[FileNameJoin[{$HomeDirectory, \"feynrules-current\"}]];  (* <-- your FeynRules folder *)
<< FeynRules`", "Input"],
Cell["2. Load the model", "Section"],
Cell["ChiEFTClearCache[] must be called right after LoadModel. Without it the pi-N-Delta vertices pick up spurious Derivative[...][HC] terms.", "Text"],
Cell["SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]];
LoadModel[\"ChiEFT.fr\"];
ChiEFTClearCache[]", "Input"],
Cell["3. Write the UFO", "Section"],
Cell["This overwrites the folder ChiEFT_UFO. It can take a while (building the Delta sector is the slow part).", "Text"],
Cell["WriteUFO[LTotal,
  AddDecays    -> False,
  FlavorExpand -> True,
  MaxParticles -> 4,
  Output       -> \"ChiEFT_UFO\"];", "Input"],
Cell["FeynRules may print warnings such as \"Form factor ... appears in more than one vertex\" or \"Cannot find particle permutation\". These are expected; the checks below confirm the result.", "Text"],
Cell["4. Quick checks", "Section"],
Cell["Expect 190 vertices, 35 form factors and no leftover Derivative/HC terms.", "Text"],
Cell["SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]];
vtx = Import[FileNameJoin[{\"ChiEFT_UFO\", \"vertices.py\"}], \"Text\"];
ffs = Import[FileNameJoin[{\"ChiEFT_UFO\", \"form_factors.py\"}], \"Text\"];
{
 \"vertices\"                         -> StringCount[vtx, \"= Vertex(\"],
 \"form factors (expect 35)\"         -> StringCount[ffs, \"= FormFactor(\"],
 \"Derivative/HC junk (expect 0)\"    -> StringCount[vtx, \"Derivative\"] + StringCount[vtx, \"HC[\"]
} // Column", "Input"],
Cell["Form factor leg check. In a form factor argument, -P(-9,n)**2 is Q^2 and needs a gauge boson (spin 3) on leg n, while +P(-9,n)**2 is the Delta's invariant mass and needs a hadron there. Expect 0 mismatches.", "Text"],
Cell["lor = Import[FileNameJoin[{\"ChiEFT_UFO\", \"lorentz.py\"}], \"Text\"];
legCheck[entry_] := Module[{spins, hits},
  spins = ToExpression /@ StringSplit[
    First@StringCases[entry, \"spins = [\" ~~ s : Except[\"]\"] .. ~~ \"]\" :> s], \",\"];
  hits = StringCases[entry,
    nm : (\"F\" ~~ WordCharacter ..) ~~ \"(\" ~~ sg : (\"-\" | \"\") ~~ \"P(-9,\" ~~
      d : DigitCharacter .. ~~ \")**2)\" :> {nm, sg, ToExpression[d]}];
  (* True when the leg type matches the sign of P^2 *)
  Table[If[h[[2]] === \"-\", spins[[h[[3]]]] === 3, spins[[h[[3]]]] =!= 3], {h, hits}]];
res = Flatten[legCheck /@ Select[StringSplit[lor, \"\\n\\n\"], StringContainsQ[#, \"P(-9,\"] &]];
{\"placements checked (40 or 41)\" -> Length[res], \"mismatches (expect 0)\" -> Count[res, False]} // Column", "Input"],
Cell["5. Write the param card", "Section"],
Cell["Writes param_card.dat with the default values stored in the UFO.", "Text"],
Cell["SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]];
Run[\"python3 -c \\\"import ChiEFT_UFO.write_param_card as w; w.ParamCardWriter('param_card.dat', generic=True)\\\"\"]
(* 0 means success *)", "Input"],
Cell["Next step: build the Sherpa model and add the form factor plugin, see README.md.", "Text"]
},
WindowSize->{900, 800},
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb"
]
